Behavior:

1. Hive may seed plan.md with a non-terminal checkpoint. If the file is missing
   or contains only that checkpoint, use the `<%= skill_invocation %>` skill to
   generate a structured plan. Required sections: `## Overview`,
   `## Requirements Trace`, `## Scope Boundaries`, `## Implementation Units`,
   `## Risks`. Each implementation unit must list goal, files, approach,
   test scenarios, and verification.
   End the plan with a trailing line `<!-- WAITING -->`.

2. If plan.md already exists, read user feedback (any inline comments or
   bullets the user added) and integrate it. End with `<!-- COMPLETE -->`
   only when no follow-up questions remain; otherwise `<!-- WAITING -->`.

Durable progress:

- Hive creates a non-terminal outline before launch. Update that checkpoint
  before extensive research or drafting, then refine it as you work. Do not hold the
  complete plan only in one long model response before the first write.
- Do not add `<!-- WAITING -->` or `<!-- COMPLETE -->` to an intermediate
  checkpoint. Those markers are terminal and belong only on the final write.
- On a retry, preserve and improve useful plan bytes already on disk; do not
  restart from an empty document merely because the prior provider stream
  ended before completion.

Constraints:
- Do not modify any file other than plan.md.
- Do not run code in the project worktree — execution happens in the next stage.
- Identify the concrete paths, symbols, and contracts each implementation unit
  assumes, and inspect them when available within your allowed context. If source
  access is unavailable, mark those assumptions unverified and require inspection
  in the execution checkout before editing; do not claim a missing prerequisite
  solely because you cannot inspect it, or block planning solely for that access
  limitation. Do not assume an architecture exists merely because another plan
  describes it. If a known unfinished task supplies a prerequisite, declare exactly one scalar
  `depends_on: <slug-or-id>` or `depends_on: <project>:<slug>` in plan.md YAML
  frontmatter. Hive adopts it into meta.yml when no dependency is already set;
  do not edit meta.yml. A conflicting existing dependency must be reconciled,
  and prose dependency statements alone are not scheduling input.
- Screenshots, recordings, and other collected outcome evidence are best-effort
  with the current tooling. Do not make unavailable historical captures or
  unsupported collection a prerequisite for implementation or completion.
  Record the missing evidence and verification limitation, use available checks,
  and keep actual product requirements and demonstrated failures actionable.
- The trailing marker must be exactly one of `<!-- WAITING -->` or
  `<!-- COMPLETE -->`.

## Completion — REQUIRED, and the last thing you do

The hive runner detects this stage ONLY from the terminal marker on the last
line of `plan.md`, never from your process exiting or returning to an idle
prompt. You are NOT done until `plan.md` ends with exactly one terminal marker —
`<!-- WAITING -->` if any follow-up question remains, otherwise the exact line
